    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1968-p21.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "For \\(k\\ge5,\\) \\(k!\\) is divisible by \\(10.\\) Only the first four terms matter. Their sum is \\(1+2+6+24=33,\\) whose units digit is \\(3.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "Every factorial from \\(5!\\) onward ends in zero",
        "Only add the units digits of the first four terms"
